<title>NORWAY: Dyno buys stake in Krems Chemie.</title>
<headline>Dyno buys stake in Krems Chemie.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian explosives and chemicals group Dyno Industrier ASA said on Friday it had acquired five percent of the shares in Austrian chemicals company Krems Chemie AG.</p>
<p>Krems Chemie has an annual turnover of around one billion crowns, Dyno said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;During the past year Dyno's chemicals business has been discussing the possibility of establishing a technical cooperation agreement with Krems Chemie covering coating resins and adhesives for the wood processing industry,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
